  "finalText": "I built the seamless 6-second ambient loop on the **Main** comp (1920×1080, 30 fps). It passed the critic with 100/100 and no loop issues.\n\n- **Blobs:** three blurred orbs, **Blob purple** (#7F5AF0), **Blob teal** (#2CB1BC) and **Blob violet** (#A855F7), on a deep navy background (#0B1026). Each drifts on a sine/cosine path with a 6 s period and breathes slightly in scale, with phase offsets so they pass each other rather than moving in step.\n- **Dot grid:** a 10×5 grid of small white dots, one group per row. Each row's opacity pulses on a 3 s period, offset row by row, so a gentle wave travels down the screen.\n\nBecause every expression is periodic over 6 s (and the 3 s pulse divides evenly into it), frame 0 and the frame after the last one match in both position and velocity. I checked frames at 0, 1.5, 3, 4.5 and 5.97 s; I did not export a video.\n\nChoices you may want to change: the dots are 6 px, which is quite subtle on a large screen, so I can make them larger or brighter. I can also add more blobs or slow the drift down."
